./critique-ledger-m9-planner-prompt.txt:154:- CL1 handoff accepted_for_cl2 is false with 5 blocking reasons, but all CL1 must-gates pass (custody, freshness, replay equality, authority, schema, prerequisite). The semantic loop gate verdict is accepted:true with zero replay failures and zero-write assertion verified. The 5 blockers are procedural/infrastructural—missing reviewer sign-off, M6 prerequisite INCOHERENT (M5 attestation gap), proof-index downstream failure, 4 Run Authority ownership blockers, portfolio gate PC-SCOPE-BLOCKER-001—not material invalidations of the frozen schemas or evidence. (source: docs/critique-ledger/handoffs/cl1-contract-oracle.json:411-441, docs/critique-ledger/evidence/cl1-semantic-loop-gate.json:51-73; relevance: high)
./critique-ledger-m9-planner-prompt.txt:156:- M6 corpus is complete (892KB, 5 rounds v1-v5, 12 artifact types per round) with overall=complete, zero missing_required_artifacts, zero unavailable_evidence. Oracle fact 6 confirms zero FAILED/DROPPED/MALFORMED instances across all rounds. The partial-parse contract is defined by the failure-atomicity-table: ParseStatus.FAILED records attempt but emits no findings; MALFORMED preserves evidence as UNAVAILABLE with reopen condition; TOMBSTONED marks record removed. LegacyClassification enum (BACKFILLED/UNKNOWN/CORRUPT/UNRECONSTRUCTABLE) enforces forward-fix-only—only has_authoritative_source permits BACKFILLED. (source: docs/critique-ledger/evidence/m6-corpus-manifest.json, docs/critique-ledger/evidence/m6-oracle.json:72-86, docs/critique-ledger/evidence/failure-atomicity-table.json, arnold/workflow/ledger_migrations.py:190-270; relevance: high)
